body:
### Tested versions

Reproducible in: 4.5.1, 4.6.dev4

### System information

Godot v4.5.1.stable - Linux Mint 21.3 (Virginia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Unknown (RADV GFX1102) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13400 (16 threads) - 31.18 GiB memory

### Issue description

This may be related or even the same as #102746 but the difference here is not just visual but the parameter values themselves are affected. I'm just getting started with shaders so apologies if this is indeed the same bug.

I made a simple color swap shader. When I changed it to use instance parameters it no longer worked correctly. After a bit of testing it appears that the actual color parameter values are wrong when passed as instance parameters. I attached a minimal example with two shaders. One shader uses instance parameters, the other doesn't. The expected result would be that the three dots in the third row are identical to the three dots in the second row. Instead the red and green dot aren't changed at all and the white dot has a different color than expected, similar to #102746.

<img width="708" height="353" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d69bbf0d-503e-4087-9acd-255a2fdcf754" />

Shader code for row 3. The shader for row 2 is identical except without the instance keyword in front of the parameters.
```
shader_type canvas_item;

instance uniform vec4 original_color: source_color;
instance uniform vec4 replacement_color: source_color;

void fragment() {
	vec4 pixel_color = texture(TEXTURE, UV);
	if (pixel_color == original_color) {
		COLOR = replacement_color;
	}
}
```

### Steps to reproduce

Run the included MRP.

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

[instanceshaderparametertest_2025-11-18_01-32-20.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23594912/instanceshaderparametertest_2025-11-18_01-32-20.zip)
